In the study, we investigate the regularizing effect of the transport operator with a discontinuous flux for the Cauchy problem of the inhomogeneous continuous velocity transport equation given by
\begin{equation*} \begin{cases} \partial_t u + v \cdot \nabla_u u = F(u) \quad\; in\; \mathbb{R}^N \times (0,T),\\ u(x,0) = u_0(x),\quad\; x\in\mathbb{R}^N. \end{cases} \label{eq:transport} \end{equal}
  We prove that a maximum fractional regularizing effect of order $s$ with $s$ greater than the sum of half the dimension of the space and one is achievable. This result is in line with the regularizing effect obtained for the transport equation with a continuous velocity.
